From 702fba1c1c9e724085f899c30dc32b1b887c89b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:26:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] test: register local capability for host stdio MCP fixtures

Remote automatic fixtures intentionally expose only their remote executor,
but these elicitation and verification tests launch host Python stdio MCP
servers. Use the existing mixed environment builder to register local
capability while retaining remote execution and thread routing.

Build the interruption fixture locally because its turn explicitly selects
local_requests with the fixture cwd. The browser-auth scenario delegates
to the repaired subagent fixture. Preserve permission checks and test
assertions. Historical native failures cover 27 affected identities;
changed-source rustfmt and diff checks pass. Native remote runtime
acceptance remains required.
